# Fable 5 can't tell you why

Bad. Fable 5, like every model anyone has measured, cannot reliably tell you why it did something. When you ask, it rereads its own output the way you would and writes a plausible story. The story is a guess. Psychology calls this confabulation, and humans do it too<Cite id="nisbett" />.

<svg viewBox="0 0 320 90" class="fig" role="img" aria-label="A straight arrow labeled 'what it says' next to a wandering path labeled 'what happened', between the same two points">
	<defs>
		<marker id="fig1-arrow" viewBox="0 0 8 8" refX="7" refY="4" markerWidth="5" markerHeight="5" orient="auto">
			<path d="M0,0 L8,4 L0,8 Z" class="fill" />
		</marker>
	</defs>
	<circle cx="20" cy="45" r="2.5" class="fill" />
	<circle cx="300" cy="45" r="2.5" class="fill" />
	<path d="M20 45 C 40 10, 60 80, 90 22 S 130 75, 160 25 S 210 70, 245 20 S 285 50, 300 45" class="stroke faint dashed" />
	<line x1="20" y1="45" x2="290" y2="45" class="stroke" marker-end="url(#fig1-arrow)" />
	<text x="62" y="12">what happened</text>
	<text x="160" y="62" text-anchor="middle">what it says</text>
</svg>

## What to do instead

- **Don't ask it why.** In Anthropic's tests<Cite id="chen" />, the model's stated reasoning mentioned the real cause 25% of the time (Claude 3.7 Sonnet; DeepSeek R1 managed 39%).
- **Don't tell it why.** Models agree with whatever you assert<Cite id="sharma" />; a bare "I don't think that's right" flips correct answers. If you supply the diagnosis and it agrees, you learned nothing.
- **Read the trace, but only for leads.** It was written during the decision, so it beats an after-the-fact answer. But that 25% was measured on the trace itself. And on [Fable 5](https://platform.claude.com/docs/en/about-claude/models/introducing-claude-fable-5) you only get a summary (`display: "summarized"`); the raw chain of thought is never returned, and prompting for it is its own refusal category, `reasoning_extraction`.
- **Trust interventions.** Think a stray TODO in context caused the bug? Delete it and rerun. An ablation can't confabulate.

<svg viewBox="0 0 320 100" class="fig" role="img" aria-label="A box with a scribble labeled 'raw trace, never returned', an arrow to a box of tidy lines labeled 'summary, what you read'">
